  "description": {
    "main": "The fourth issue of the irregular journal Bricks from the Kiln, which approaches graphic design and typography through other disciplines. This issue takes translation, transmission and transposition as its subject and muses on the colour green.",
    "extended": "<p>An issue of an irregular journal on graphic design and typography. This one is organised around translation, transmission and transposition.</p><p class=\"mt-6\">Bricks from the Kiln #4 is a 288-page softcover with an insert. It is printed in one-colour offset in a run of 1,000 copies and muses on the colour green. It came out as both an event and a publication. Contributors include Helen Marten, Sophie Collins, Don Mee Choi, Kate Briggs and Caroline Bergvall.</p><p class=\"mt-6\">The journal takes its name from Ret Marut's anarchist magazine <em>Der Ziegelbrenner</em>, published from 1917 to 1921. This issue was edited by Natalie Ferris, Bryony Quinn, Matthew Stuart and Andrew Walsh-Lister.</p>",
